els, traversal, packing_density, link_detectors, architecture, muon_optimizer, generation_retrieval, eval_harness, training_loop, data_pipelines, merged_multisource) are subsystem summaries **pinned to a commit** with an explicit drift check. E.g. `paper/notes/code_briefs/architecture.md:1-7`: `&lt;!-- PROVENANCE ... Covered sources: model/modules/backbone.py ... --&gt;` and `paper/notes/code_briefs/README.md:11-16`: *\"git diff --stat &lt;pin-commit&gt;..HEAD -- &lt;covered paths&gt; ... Empty output ⇒ the brief is still faithful to the code.\"*\n- **Deep-dives** (`paper/notes/deepdives/*.md`, ~25 files, one per related-work paper, e.g. `gutierrez2024hipporag.md`) cite bib keys and cross-reference code briefs (`\"Our-side claims verified against the code briefs generation_retrieval.md, eval_harness.md, traversal.md...\"`).\n- **Citation graph**: `paper/bib/refs.bib` (533 entries) is cited via `\\cite{key}` from `paper/sections/*.tex`; `paper/notes/deepdives/missed_citation_candidates.md` tracks candidate edges not yet in the bib, tagged HIGH/MED/LOW and grouped by source paper.\n- **Numeric grounding (the real DAG)**: `provenance/README.md` + `provenance/ledger.yaml` define claim-key → run-record-field mappings, resolved into `paper/generated/values.tex` (`\\valdef{key}{value}`, cited as `\\val{key}` in prose). This is edge-typed: `eval {metric_path, field}`, `hyperparam {path}`, `derived {op, operands}` (a DAG over other claim-keys), `literal {value}` (flagged as \"grounding debt\"). Serialization: YAML ledger + JSON run records + generated `.tex` lockfile — not JSON-graph/sqlite.\n- Not a general graph store — it's a set of one-way pointers (brief→commit+paths, claim-key→run+field, tex→claim-key) checked by scripts (`scripts/check_grounding.py`, `scripts/distill_runs.py`, `scripts/gen_values_tex.py`, `provenance/README.md:23-31`), not a queryable node/edge database.\n- No reference anywhere to `conversation-ledger`, `cledger`, or `context-graph` (`grep -rliE \"cledger|conversation-ledger|context-graph\" .` returned nothing).\n\n## 2. Training code — TAGSeq2TAGSeq\n\nDespite the name reading like \"tag sequences,\" `README.md:1` clarifies: **\"Text Attributed Graph Sequence to Text Attributed Graph Sequence\"** — TAG = Text-Attributed Graph, i.e. a corpus where documents are nodes and hyperlinks/imports/citations are edges (`README.md:3,94-100`: SimpleWiki/EnWikiSource via Markdown hyperlinks, The Stack via Python `import`, arXiv via `\\cite{}`). It's a graph-structured-pretraining project, not a POS/label-tagging model. Node/edge structure lives in the training data itself (traversal strategies BFS/DFS/random-walk over the doc-link graph, `README.md:75-84`) and in custom attention masks (`doc_causal`, `cross_doc_link`, `doc_concat_link`, `doc_concatenated`, `README.md:21-71`).\n\n**Lineage tracking is real and DAG-shaped**, in `provenance/`: each training run produces one `provenance/runs/&lt;run_id&gt;.json` record (`schema_version`, `run_id`, git `commit_hash`/dirty flag + a content-addressed `patches/&lt;sha256&gt;.patch` for uncommitted diffs, resolved `hyperparameters` including `config_path` and `dataset_dir`, environment, and `eval.metrics`). Runs link to prior runs via `reproduce.cli_overrides[\"resume-from\"]` pointing at another run's checkpoint path (e.g. `provenance/runs/run_20260819_144147_693022.json`: `\"resume-from\": \"runs/run_20260818_020329_564573/checkpoints/latest.pt\"`), forming a checkpoint-resumption chain. Artifacts per run: git commit + patch, config, checkpoints, eval metrics JSON — linked run→config, run→patch, run→parent-run (via checkpoint), run→claim-key (via `ledger.yaml`). Capture side is an external package (`tunalab.reproducibility.ReproducibilityManager`, `provenance/README.md:60-63`); this repo's tools only read/distill/check.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>36197</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>16</tool_uses><duration_ms>200737</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","type":"text"}]