hipporag.md`) cite bib keys and cross-reference code briefs (`\"Our-side claims verified against the code briefs generation_retrieval.md, eval_harness.md, traversal.md...\"`).\n- **Citation graph**: `paper/bib/refs.bib` (533 entries) is cited via `\\cite{key}` from `paper/sections/*.tex`; `paper/notes/deepdives/missed_citation_candidates.md` tracks candidate edges not yet in the bib, tagged HIGH/MED/LOW and grouped by source paper.\n- **Numeric grounding (the real DAG)**: `provenance/README.md` + `provenance/ledger.yaml` define claim-key → run-record-field mappings, resolved into `paper/generated/values.tex` (`\\valdef{key}{value}`, cited as `\\val{key}` in prose). This is edge-typed: `eval {metric_path, field}`, `hyperparam {path}`, `derived {op, operands}` (a DAG over other claim-keys), `literal {value}` (flagged as \"grounding debt\"). Serialization: YAML ledger + JSON run records + generated `.tex` lockfile — not JSON-graph/sqlite.\n- Not a general graph store — it's a set of one-way pointers (brief→commit+paths, claim-key→run+field, tex→claim-key) checked by scripts (`scripts/check_grounding.py`, `scripts/distill_runs.py`, `scripts/gen_values_tex.py`, `provenance/README.md:23-31`), not a queryable node/edge database.\n- No reference anywhere to `conversation-ledger`, `cledger`, or `context-graph` (`grep -rliE \"cledger|conversation-ledger|context-graph\" .` returned nothing).\n\n## 2. Training code — TAGSeq2TAGSeq\n\nDespite the name reading like \"tag sequences,\" `README.md:1` clarifies: **\"Text Attributed Graph Sequence to Text Attributed Graph Sequence\"** — TAG = Text-Attributed Graph, i.e. a corpus where documents are nodes and hyperlinks/imports/citations are edges (`README.md:3,94-100`: SimpleWiki/EnWikiSource via Markdown hyperlinks, The Stack via Python `import`, arXiv via `\\cite{}`). It's a graph-structured-pretraining project, not a POS/label-tagging model. Node/edge structure lives in the training data itself (traversal strategies BFS/DFS/random-