{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"(`store.ts:318`). A filter option therefore saves *zero* I/O — it is pure\nergonomics, and any consumer can already express any of these as\n`events.filter(...)` itself. That argues for adding filters with a cited\nconsumer need and resisting speculative ones, since public API surface is\ncheap to add and permanent to keep.\n\n**Add — each backed by real consumer code:**\n\n- **`tool?: string`** — exact match on `producer.tool`. Required by the\n  Decision 2 pair-key contract; without it the pair is not addressable.\n- **`kind?: string | string[]`** — widen the existing exact-match. turnbridge\n  carries an explicit workaround comment for its absence\n  (`conversations.ts:36-38`): *\"readEvents' `kind` filter is exact-match only,\n  so fetch everything and narrow here rather than issuing two reads.\"* It needs\n  `conversation_turn` **or** `reasoning`. This also subsumes any\n  \"hide/show session machinery\" filtering, since `SESSION_MACHINERY_KINDS` is\n  just a set of kinds.\n- **`linkRel?: string`** — match events carrying a `links[].rel`. context-graph's\n  design extracts its `continuation` edge from `rel:\"continues\"`, and\n  turnbridge's `readLineage` currently reads by kind and parses. Graph\n  consumers want edges by relation, which is the one query shape no existing\n  filter expresses.\n\n**Considered and deferred, with reasons** (add when a consumer actually asks):\n\n- `actorId` — turnbridge's ownership filter is \"mine **or** unattributed\",\n  which an exact-match cannot express, so it would not actually remove the\n  client-side pass it was meant to serve.\n- `since`/`until` — no consumer has asked, and it would need to resolve the\n  `occurred_at` vs `recorded_at` ambiguity to be meaningful.\n- `producerVersion` — a consumer handling two vocabulary revisions reads both\n  and branches on the version; filtering it out is the rarer need.\n\nAlso worth stating in the docs, since it is the tradeoff being accepted: two\nevents differing *only* by `producer.tool` dedup to one, because `producer.tool`\nis not in identity. That is the correct behavior — byte-identical content is the\nsame fact — but it should be documented rather than discovered.\n\n## Decision 3 — migration mechanism (not needed now, but named)\n\nDecision 2 removes the migration. The pattern is recorded here anyway, because","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RcyHAJQEDhHHcqpybnVcdN","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"324e5de5bd856853a4c994915cf2b93c8a3d6e6b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-d3d6b36d6ada573254c96bee93ab3fc68ca736c84c4b25e69bca662fc53c6025","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.241"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-24T02:18:25.726Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"(`store.ts:318`). A filter option therefore saves *zero* I/O — it is pure\nergonomics, and any consumer can already express any of these as\n`events.filter(...)` itself. That argues for adding filters with a cited\nconsumer need and resisting speculative ones, since public API surface is\ncheap to add and permanent to keep.\n\n**Add — each backed by real consumer code:**\n\n- **`tool?: string`** — exact match on `producer.tool`. Required by the\n  Decision 2 pair-key contract; without it the pair is not addressable.\n- **`kind?: string | string[]`** — widen the existing exact-match. turnbridge\n  carries an explicit workaround comment for its absence\n  (`conversations.ts:36-38`): *\"readEvents' `kind` filter is exact-match only,\n  so fetch everythi