{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Code briefs\n2\t\n3\tTwelve line-referenced technical summaries of the TAGSeq2TAGSeq subsystems, written\n4\tto ground the paper (method section + appendices) in the actual implementation. Each\n5\tbrief distills one subsystem: what it does, the exact mechanism, concrete parameters,\n6\tand reviewer-relevant subtleties.\n7\t\n8\t## Staleness / drift protocol\n9\tThese briefs are a snapshot of the code, so they go stale as the code evolves. Each\n10\tfile starts with a `<!-- PROVENANCE -->` header recording (a) the commit it was\n11\twritten against and (b) the source paths it covers, with a ready-to-run drift check:\n12\t\n13\t    git diff --stat <pin-commit>..HEAD -- <covered paths>\n14\t\n15\tEmpty output ⇒ the brief is still faithful to the code. Non-empty ⇒ the covered\n16\tsources moved; re-verify the affected claims against source (or regenerate the brief)\n17\tbefore relying on it. All briefs were pinned to the same commit, `6134163` (main,\n18\t2026-08-07). To check every brief at once:\n19\t\n20\t    for f in *.md; do\n21\t      paths=$(sed -n 's/^Covered sources: //p' \"$f\")\n22\t      [ -n \"$paths\" ] && { echo \"== $f ==\"; git diff --stat 6134163..HEAD -- $paths; }\n23\t    done\n24\t\n25\t## Contents\n26\tmasks, kernels, traversal, packing_density, link_detectors, architecture,\n27\tmuon_optimizer, generation_retrieval, eval_harness, training_loop, data_pipelines,\n28\tmerged_multisource.\n29\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_0129Pie5cuEGF23sy6nS1JjS","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"324e5de5bd856853a4c994915cf2b93c8a3d6e6b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-242237c8c91af4ad380447f536ee060207a0f21fe34df4ddfe22bb0485718bd7","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"system"},"session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.241"