lAssistantUUID":"a978aa1b-0e92-4eb2-b79f-6da3c36bd18b","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:25:04.972Z","toolUseResult":{"file":{"content":"# Code briefs\n\nTwelve line-referenced technical summaries of the TAGSeq2TAGSeq subsystems, written\nto ground the paper (method section + appendices) in the actual implementation. Each\nbrief distills one subsystem: what it does, the exact mechanism, concrete parameters,\nand reviewer-relevant subtleties.\n\n## Staleness / drift protocol\nThese briefs are a snapshot of the code, so they go stale as the code evolves. Each\nfile starts with a `<!-- PROVENANCE -->` header recording (a) the commit it was\nwritten against and (b) the source paths it covers, with a ready-to-run drift check:\n\n    git diff --stat <pin-commit>..HEAD -- <covered paths>\n\nEmpty output ⇒ the brief is still faithful to the code. Non-empty ⇒ the covered\nsources moved; re-verify the affected claims against source (or regenerate the brief)\nbefore relying on it. All briefs were pinned to the same commit, `6134163` (main,\n2026-08-07). To check every brief at once:\n\n    for f in *.md; do\n      paths=$(sed -n 's/^Covered sources: //p' \"$f\")\n      [ -n \"$paths\" ] && { echo \"== $f ==\"; git diff --stat 6134163..HEAD -- $paths; }\n    done\n\n## Contents\nmasks, kernels, traversal, packing_density, link_detectors, architecture,\nmuon_optimizer, generation_retrieval, eval_harness, training_loop, data_pipelines,\nmerged_multisource.\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq/paper/notes/code_briefs/README.md","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29},"type":"text"},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"d4a9319f-8bc5-415e-afdb-c541db2f2305","version":"2.1.241"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-24T03:27:55.245Z","schema":"annals/v1","stream":{"id":"claude-code:a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87#agent:a0468aee6692a7819","parent":"claude-code:a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","seq":23}}
{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Provenance: keeping the paper's numbers grounded\n2\t\n3\tEvery result number in `paper/` must trace to the run — and the exact code + config\n4\tstate — that produced it. `runs/` is gitignored and ephemeral, so this tracked tree is\n5\tthe durable record. Numbers reach the paper by *generation*, not by hand-typing, so they\n6\tcannot silently drift as prose is edited.\n7\t\n8\t## What's here\n9\t\n10\t- `runs/<run_id>.json` — one distilled, self-contained record per run: git commit + dirty\n11\t  flag, config path + CLI overrides, resolved hyperparameters, python/torch/cuda/driver +\n12\t  GPU/world-size, timestamps, and a verbatim copy of that run's eval metrics. Survives\n13\t  deletion of the ephemeral run dir.\n14\t- `patches/<sha256>.patch` — content-addressed store of the uncommitted diff for every\n15\t  git-dirty run (deduped by hash). Reproduce a dirty run with:\n16\t  `git checkout <commit_hash> && git apply provenance/patches/<hash>.patch`.\n17\t- `ledger.yaml` — the curated map from a stable claim-key to a *value source* (a specific\n18\t  field of a specific run's record). The single source of truth for paper numbers.\n19\t\n20\tThe generated `paper/generated/values.tex` (a committed lockfile) binds each claim-key to\n21\tits resolved value as `\\valdef{key}{value}`; the paper cites `\\val{key}`.\n22\t\n23\t## Tools (`scripts/`)\n24\t\n25\t- `distill_runs.py` — harvest run dirs (both `runs/` and the `/fss-data` runs root) into\n26\t  `runs/` + `patches/`. Idempotent; safe to run anytime (cron / pre-push).\n27\t- `gen_values_tex.py` — resolve the ledger and (re)write `paper/generated/values.tex`.\n28\t  All-or-nothing: any unresolvable entry aborts with a nonzero exit and names the key.\n29\t- `check_grounding.py` — the drift gate (wire into pre-push / CI). Verifies the ledger\n30\t  resolves and matches `expected`, that `values.tex` is fresh, that every `\\val{}` in the\n31\t  paper has a ledger key, run-dir liveness, and patch integrity.\n32\t- `provenance_lib.py` — shared resolver used by both the generator and the checker (so they\n33\t  can never disagree).\n34\t\n35\t## Adding a grounded number (end to end)\n36\t\n37\t1. Run finishes → `python scripts/distill_runs.py` (records + patches refresh; a later\n38\t   re-eval is picked up automatically via the metrics hash).\n39\t2. Add an entry to `ledger.yaml`: a `claim-key`, its `run_ids`, a `source`\n40\t   (`eval` / `hyperparam` / `literal`), optional `expected`, and a `format`.\n41\t3. `python scripts/gen_values_tex.py` → regenerate and commit `paper/generated/values.tex`.\n42\t4. Cite it in prose: replace the hand-typed number (inside a `\\todo{}`) with `\\val{claim-key}`.\n43\t5. `python scripts/check_grounding.py` must pass before pushing.\n44\t\n45\t## Value sources\n46\t\n47\t- `eval {metric_path, field}` — reads `record.eval.metrics[metric_path][field]`. For a\n48\t  confidence interval, use an array field (`accuracy_ci`) or a `<base>_ci` field; the\n49\t  resolver also accepts sibling `<base>_ci_low`/`<base>_ci_high` scalars and normalizes\n50\t  both to `[lo, hi]` (set `format.kind: interval`).\n51\t- `hyperparam {path}` — dotted lookup into `record.hyperparameters`.\n52\t- `literal {value}` — escape hatch for a number NOT in any distilled artifact (e.g. read\n53\t  from a training log). **Requires a `note`.** These are *grounding debt*: `check_grounding.py`\n54\t  lists them in a separate \"declared but ungrounded\" bucket for reverification at\n55\t  camera-ready. Prefer grounding to a real source; a `kind: log` source (parse\n56\t  `runs/<id>/logs/`) is the intended future replacement.\n57\t\n58\t## Notes\n59\t\n60\t- The capture side (`tunalab.reproducibility.ReproducibilityManager`, an external editable\n61\t  package) writes each run's `reproducibility/` + `hyperparameters.json` +\n62\t  `eval_results.json`. The tools here only *read* those — they never modify run dirs or the\n63\t  package.\n64\t- Records for deleted run dirs are kept, never removed; `distill_runs.py --prune-missing`\n65\t  flips their `run_dir_exists` to `false` so the checker stops warning.\n66\t- The ledger currently ships `example.*` schema-demonstration entries (they exercise every\n67\t  resolver path against real runs). Replace them with real curated claims as the paper's\n68\t  `\\todo{}` numbers are grounded.\n69\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01FU6QTjqGo9uieMDSRvhuW2","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"324e5de5bd856853a4c994915cf2b93c8a3d6e6b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-3ead852cd3940a9b4a3829f3142e999bb969fa623028ea6bc48a5b5871d1aef0","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"system"},"session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.241"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-24T03:25:37.169Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a0468aee6692a7819","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":[{"content":"1\t# Provenance: keeping the paper's numbers grounded\n2\t\n3\tEvery result number in `paper/` must trace to the run — and the exact code + config\n4\tstate — that produced it. `runs/` is gitignored and ephemeral, so this tracked tree is\n5\tthe durable record. Numbers reach the paper by *generation*, not by hand-typing, so they\n6\tcannot silently drift as prose is edited.\n7\t\n8\t## What's here\n9\t\n10\t- `runs/<run_id>.json` — one distilled, self-contained record per run: git commit + dirty\n11\t  flag, config path + CLI overrides, resolved hyperparameters, python/torch/cuda/driver +\n12\t  GPU/world-size, timestamps, and a verbatim copy of that run's eval metrics. Survives\n13\t  deletion of the ephemeral run dir.\n14\t- `patches/<sha256>.patch` — content-addressed store