oc_concat_link mask on The Stack](docs/images/mask_doc_concat_link.png)\n\n*Same batch as `cross_doc_link` above. Each grant block now extends up to the top of its source file — compare the tall bottom-left block here against the shorter one in the previous figure, which started at the import line.*\n\n---\n\n### `doc_concatenated` — connected-component concatenation (compute control)\n\nDocuments that form a connected component in the link graph (e.g. files within a repository that import one another) are merged into a single causally-concatenated super-document: full causal attention across their combined tokens. Components that share no links remain isolated, so the mask is a block-diagonal of *larger* triangles — one per component, not one per document.\n\n![doc_concatenated mask on The Stack](docs/images/mask_doc_concatenated.png)\n\n*All files in this batch are import-connected, so they merge into a single super-document triangle — the per-file boundaries (blue dashed lines) are ignored entirely. Had the batch contained an unrelated, unlinked file, it would sit in its own separate triangle.*\n\nThis grants the most attention of the four conditions, with no inference-time linking — the upper compute control.\n\n---\n\n## Graph Traversal\n\nHow documents are ordered within a sequence matters for `cross_doc_link`: a document can only attend to documents that appear *before* it in the sequence. The traversal strategy controls this ordering.\n\n- **BFS** (breadth-first): explores the neighbourhood of a seed document level by level. Documents close in graph distance are packed together and predecessors tend to appear before successors. This is the preferred strategy for `cross_doc_link` training.\n- **DFS** (depth-first): follows one path deep into the graph before backtracking. Produces longer chains of topically related documents.\n- **Random walk**: a Markov walk with restart probability, producing soft locality without strict BFS ordering.\n- **Random**: uniform random selection — equivalent to standard document sampling, used as a control baseline.\n\nWithin each strategy, a token budget and per-document token cap control sequence length and ensure no single document dominates the pack.\n\n---\n\n## Datasets\n\nThe framework currently supports four pretokenized datasets and has several more in progress, spanning three distinct link-structure modalities.\n\n### Ready\n\n| Dataset | Edge type | Nodes | Tokens |\n|---------|-----------|-------|--------|\n| **SimpleWiki** | Markdown hyperlinks | 275k | ~108M |\n| **EnWikiSource** | Markdown hyperlinks | 662k | ~612M |\n| **The Stack** | Python `import` statements | 3.56M | ~8.7B |\n| **arXiv (unarXive 2024)** | `\\cite{}` citations | 2.20M | ~10B |\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq/README.md","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":232},"type":"text"},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"d373c42a-fbae-4689-bacd-cf898f2df613","version":"2.1.241"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-24T03:27:55.246Z","schema":"annals/v1","stream":{"id":"claude-code:a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87#agent:a0468aee6692a7819","parent":"claude-code:a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","seq":32}}
{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\timport { appendEvents, readEvents, type EvidenceEvent, type RepoInfo } from \"conversation-ledger\";\n2\t\n3\tconst CONTINUATION_KIND = \"continuation\";\n4\tconst CONTINUES_REL = \"continues\";\n5\t\n6\texport interface ContinuationRecord {\n7\t  /** Conversation that was bridged from (the ancestor). */\n8\t  source: string;\n9\t  /** Conversation the bridge created (the descendant tip). */\n10\t  target: string;\n11\t  /** Highest source seq copied into the target at bridge time. */\n12\t  importedThroughSeq: number;\n13\t  /** Target CLI the bridge fabricated into. */\n14\t  targetCli: string;\n15\t  occurredAt: string;\n16\t}\n17\t\n18\texport interface Lineage {\n19\t  /** target conversation id -> its continuation record (one parent). */\n20\t  parentOf: Map<string, ContinuationRecord>;\n21\t  /** source conversation id -> continuation records that descend from it. */\n22\t  childrenOf: Map<string, ContinuationRecord[]>;\n23\t}\n24\t\n25\t/**\n26\t * Record that `target` was fabricated as a continuation of `source`. Stored as\n27\t * a ledger event so the edge travels and syncs with the conversations it\n28\t * links, using conversation-ledger's `links` extension point.\n29\t */\n30\texport async function recordContinuation(\n31\t  repo: RepoInfo,\n32\t  rec: Omit<ContinuationRecord, \"occurredAt\"> & { version: string },\n33\t): Promise<void> {\n34\t  const occurredAt = new Date().toISOString();\n35\t  await appendEvents(repo, [\n36\t    {\n37\t      kind: CONTINUATION_KIND,\n38\t      occurred_at: occurredAt,\n39\t      actor: { type: \"system\", id: \"turnbridge\" },\n40\t      producer: { tool: \"turnbridge\", version: rec.version, source: rec.targetCli },\n41\t      // belongs to the target conversation so it rides along with it\n42\t      conversation: { id: rec.target, seq: 0 },\n43\t      links: [{ rel: CONTINUES_REL, target: rec.source }],\n44\t      content: {\n45\t        source_conversation: rec.source,\n46\t        target_conversation: rec.target,\n47\t        imported_through_seq: rec.importedThroughSeq,\n48\t        target_cli: rec.targetCli,\n49\t      },\n50\t    },\n51\t  ]);\n52\t}\n53\t\n54\tfunction parseRecord(event: EvidenceEvent): ContinuationRecord | null {\n55\t  const c = event.content as Record<string, unknown> | null;\n56\t  if (!c || typeof c !== \"object\") return null;\n57\t  const source = c[\"source_conversation\"];\n58\t  const target = c[\"target_conversation\"];\n59\t  if (typeof source !== \"string\" || typeof target !== \"string\") return null;\n60\t  return {\n61\t    source,\n62\t    target,\n63\t    importedThroughSeq: typeof c[\"imported_through_seq\"] === \"number\" ? c[\"imported_through_seq\"] : 0,\n64\t    targetCli: typeof c[\"target_cli\"] === \"string\" ? c[\"target_cli\"] : \"unknown\",\n65\t    occurredAt: event.occurred_at,\n66\t  };\n67\t}\n68\t\n69\texport async function readLineage(repo: RepoInfo, anyCommit = false): Promise<Lineage> {\n70\t  const events = await readEvents(repo, {\n71\t    kind: CONTINUATION_KIND,\n72\t    ...(anyCommit ? {} : { reachableFrom: \"HEAD\" }),\n73\t  });\n74\t  const parentOf = new Map<string, ContinuationRecord>();\n75\t  const childrenOf = new Map<string, ContinuationRecord[]>();\n76\t  for (const event of events) {\n77\t    const rec = parseRecord(event);\n78\t    if (!rec) continue;\n79\t    parentOf.set(rec.target, rec);\n80\t    const list = childrenOf.get(rec.source);\n81\t    if (list) list.push(rec);\n82\t    else childrenOf.set(rec.source, [rec]);\n83\t  }\n84\t  return { parentOf, childrenOf };\n85\t}\n86\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nk2jWb197secmWiAwQJgJq","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"324e5de5bd856853a4c994915cf2b93c8a3d6e6b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-849c462e280dbfe4bc17e2f77ab30bb2028819698f209578aea9adbdfecb8c32","kind":"conversation_tu