{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Statements that clearly target another project cannot be routed (see D8) and are\nparked in a visible unrouted bucket rather than dropped or misapplied.\n\n## Storage\n\n**D10. The intent tree is committed to the repository and mirrors the source tree.**\nConversation Ledger uses git notes because it stores raw evidence, where there is\nnothing to review beyond a secret scan. The intent layer is different: it is\nderived, it is exactly what a human should review and hand-correct, and it should\nappear in PR diffs. Mirroring the source tree also makes folder-chain scoping\n(D9) a path-prefix walk, and follows the existing repository convention that\ntests, configs, and todo files mirror the code they concern.\n\n**D11. Storage is pointers and verbatim spans, never model-authored prose.**\nEach record is a pointer into Conversation Ledger (event id + span), the verbatim\ntext of that span denormalized for reviewability, a content hash for\nverification against the ledger, and typed edges. A model may decide *what to\nselect*; it may never author the payload. Summarization would reintroduce the\ncorrelated model error the project exists to remove.\n\n**D12. Machine format, not Markdown; human readability comes from a renderer.**\nThe intent tree is not a document. It is a line-oriented, append-friendly,\ngit-diffable record. Verbatim quotes (D11) keep PR diffs legible without any\nprose being authored.\n\n**D13. Never append derived data to Conversation Ledger.**\nIntent Recall maintains its own append-only log, separate from the ledger ref.\nTwo reasons: writing derived output into the source substrate destroys the\nability to regenerate from a clean base (D14), and it creates a feedback loop in\nwhich a later extraction pass reads its own prior output as historical evidence —\nthe correlated-error failure in its purest form. This must be architecturally\nimpossible, not merely discouraged.\n\n**D14. The intent tree is fully regenerable, and the extractor is versioned.**\nThe derived layer is a pure function of (ledger events, extractor version,\nhuman corrections). Deleting and rebuilding it must be lossless. Every record\ncarries the extractor version that produced it, and re-migration to a newer\nextractor is a first-class supported operation. This is what makes a mediocre\nv1 selection algorithm acceptable: it is explicitly swappable, and nothing about\nit is permanent.\n\n**D15. Human corrections are stored separately from derived content.**\nA consequence of D14: if corrections lived inside the derived tree, regeneration\nwould destroy them. Corrections are their own append-only record and are\nreplayed on top of a regenerated tree.\n\n## Selection\n\n**D16. Compress the selection, not the text.**\nA bad index costs recall — a missed quote. A bad summary costs fidelity — a\nplausible fabricated quote. Only the second reintroduces correlated error, so\nmodels may be used aggressively for selection provided the payload stays\nverbatim (D11).\n\n**D17. Extraction is amortized per event at write time, not per query.**\nThe ledger is append-only, so index maintenance is O(new events). History is\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_013WVVEuzxMRfikxf3PpyJh5","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"324e5de5bd856853a4c994915cf2b93c8a3d6e6b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-e3bb3de7d2b855e344ce300675e77cef352db48e2471830b6d0bd553c8070107","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.241"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-24T03:23:26.889Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/rep