{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"Memento \"Git extension for AI session tracking\" git notes\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Releases · mandel-macaque/memento\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mandel-macaque/memento/releases\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - mandel-macaque/memento: Keep track of you codex sessions per commit · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mandel-macaque/memento\"},{\"title\":\"git-memento-note-comment - GitHub Marketplace\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marketplace/actions/git-memento-note-comment\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - git-ai-project/git-ai: A Git extension for tracking the AI-generated code in your repos · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-ai-project/git-ai\"},{\"title\":\"Agent Sessions Are the Real Commit Messages We Discard\",\"url\":\"https://blakecrosley.com/blog/session-is-the-commit-message\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - scrypster/memento: Persistent memory for AI tools — give every session the context of every session before it.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/scrypster/memento\"},{\"title\":\"Git AI - Track AI Code all the way to production\",\"url\":\"https://usegitai.com/\"}]\n\nI found information about Memento and AI session tracking with Git. Here are the search results:\n\n## Memento - Git Extension for AI Session Tracking\n\nMemento is a Git extension that captures AI coding session context and attaches it to commits as git notes, so teams can audit and understand how changes were produced.\n\n### Key Features\n\nMemento creates normal Git commits while attaching AI session transcripts as commit notes, supports multi-session notes (including amend/append flows), and helps teams share and sync notes across remotes.\n\nIt supports Codex and Claude provider configuration via local git config.\n\n### Basic Commands\n\nThe main commands include `git memento init` to initialize repository-level memento configuration, and `git memento commit <session-id>` to create a commit and attach the AI session note.\n\n### 