{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"beads steveyegge issue tracker git storage JSONL agents how it syncs\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - Dicklesworthstone/beads_rust: Fast Rust port of Steve Yegge's beads: local-first, non-invasive issue tracker storing tasks in SQLite with JSONL export for git collaboration · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/beads_rust\"},{\"title\":\"Beads: A Git-Friendly Issue Tracker for AI Coding Agents | Better Stack Community\",\"url\":\"https://betterstack.com/community/guides/ai/beads-issue-tracker-ai-agents/\"},{\"title\":\"beads package - github.com/steveyegge/beads - Go Packages\",\"url\":\"https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/steveyegge/beads\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - gastownhall/beads: Beads - A memory upgrade for your coding agent · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/gastownhall/beads\"},{\"title\":\"Beads - Memory for your Agent and The Best Damn Issue Tracker Your're Not Using\",\"url\":\"https://ianbull.com/posts/beads/\"},{\"title\":\"The Beads Revolution: How I Built The TODO System That AI Agents Actually Want to Use | by Steve Yegge | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://steve-yegge.medium.com/the-beads-revolution-how-i-built-the-todo-system-that-ai-agents-actually-want-to-use-228a5f9be2a9\"},{\"title\":\"Beads | Peter Warnock\",\"url\":\"https://peterwarnock.com/tools/beads-distributed-task-management-for-agents/\"},{\"title\":\"opencode beads\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/joshuadavidthomas/opencode-beads\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Beads, Steve Yegge's issue tracker, and how it syncs:\n\n## Storage Architecture\n\nBeads uses a local SQLite database (beads.db) stored within a .beads folder in your project directory, which holds all issues, their statuses, priorities, descriptions, and relationships.\n\n## Git Synchronization via JSONL\n\nBeads solves the problem of storing binary SQLite files in Git with a companion file: issues.jsonl. JSON-L (JSON Lines) is a text format where each line represents a valid JSON object. When changes occur in the SQLite database, a background daemon automatically exports changes as new lines in the issues.jsonl file.\n\nHowever, cross-machine sync uses bd dolt push / bd dolt pull against refs/dolt/data on your git remote; .beads/issues.jsonl is an export for viewers and interchange, not the source of truth or a backup.\n\n## Agent Synchronization Workflow\n\nBehind the scenes, a background daemon handles synchronization: CLI Command → Unix Socket → Daemon → SQLite DB ↓ JSONL Export (5s debounce) ↓ Git commit/push (if enabled).\n\nFor multi-agent coordination, each agent gets its own worktree and branch, Beads syncs via git, and agents work independently and merge normally.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DfZ4RJVYA2pyRXD5MTqMNS","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"324e5de5bd856853a4c994915cf2b93c8a3d6e6b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-6fbbd923ef8ff815fea58b3580952fef9e988d005ae63c79555121f951b354a6","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.241"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-24T03:44:51.415Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"beads steveyegge issue tracker git storage JSONL agents how it syncs\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - Dicklesworthstone/beads_rust: Fast Rust port of Steve Yegge's beads: local-first, non-invasive issue tracker storing tasks in SQLite with JSONL ex