{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"dolt \"refs/dolt/data\" git remote push pull versioned database beads\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Dolt Remote Federation | steveyegge/beads | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/steveyegge/beads/9.3-dolt-remote-federation\"},{\"title\":\"beads package - github.com/steveyegge/beads - Go Packages\",\"url\":\"https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/steveyegge/beads\"},{\"title\":\"Supporting Git remotes as Dolt remotes | DoltHub Blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.dolthub.com/blog/2026-02-19-supporting-git-remotes-as-dolt-remotes/\"},{\"title\":\"beads/website/versioned_docs/version-1.0.5/reference/git-integration.md at main · gastownhall/beads\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/blob/main/website/versioned_docs/version-1.0.5/reference/git-integration.md\"},{\"title\":\"How to actually commit beads to git history now that JSONL is out of the picture? · gastownhall/beads · Discussion #2332\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/discussions/2332\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Git remote support in Dolt | DoltHub Blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.dolthub.com/blog/2026-02-13-announcing-git-remote-support-in-dolt/\"},{\"title\":\"Using Remotes - Dolt Documentation - DoltHub\",\"url\":\"https://docs.dolthub.com/sql-reference/version-control/remotes\"},{\"title\":\"Dolt Backend for Beads - Beads Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://beads.gascity.com/architecture/dolt\"},{\"title\":\"Configure beads dolt to share via git | bjorn.now\",\"url\":\"https://bjorn.now/til/2026-03-20-configure-beads-dolt-to-share-via-git/\"}]\n\nI found relevant search results about Dolt, Git remotes, and Beads. Here's what the search reveals:\n\n## Overview\n\nDolt v1.81.10 lets you use Git remotes as Dolt remotes — store and sync versioned SQL databases alongside your code via the Dolt CLI and Dolt sql-server.\n\n## How refs/dolt/data Works\n\nDolt stores data under refs/dolt/data, separate from Git refs, meaning beads data doesn't conflict with protected Git branches — no special branch flag is needed. By default Dolt uses refs/dolt/data, but you can override this with --ref.\n\n## Push/Pull Operations\n\nUnlike Git remotes (which sync the entire refs/dolt/data branch), Dolt remotes operate at the SQL database level and support incremental push/pull operations. Cross-machine sync uses bd dolt push and bd dolt pull against refs/dolt/data.\n\n## Beads Integration\n\nThis makes it possible to push your Dolt database to remotes like GitHub, so your version-controlled SQL database can use the same repository as your source code, supporting the transition of Beads from SQLite to Dolt.\n\nDolt remotes enable push/pull replication between beads databases using Dolt's version control protocol.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01VrFcXQACTvTK2mD1FTNWoY","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"324e5de5bd856853a4c994915cf2b93c8a3d6e6b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-a6ec1b2dff5922652936683366d01c74e3e2d087231911bb1583cd545dfbd420","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.241"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-24T03:45:25.445Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"dolt \"refs/dolt/data\" git remote push pull versioned database beads\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Dolt Remote Federation | steveyegge/beads | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/steveyegge/beads/9.3-dolt-remote-federation\"},{\"title\":\"beads pack