{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"git-bug entity operations DAG stored in git refs generic entity framework\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Releases · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MichaelMure/git-bug/releases\"},{\"title\":\"git-bug/entity/dag/example_test.go at master · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/blob/master/entity/dag/example_test.go\"},{\"title\":\"Identity management · Issue #55 · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/55\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - OfferingSolutions/Entity-Framework-Core-Generic-Repository: Offering you a complete abstraction of the UnitOfWork-Pattern with the basic CRUD-Operations, the Repository Pattern and extended functions like CustomRepositores all in one small lib. Made for the Entity Framework Core. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/OfferingSolutions/Entity-Framework-Core-Generic-Repository\"},{\"title\":\"Git Bug: Distributed, Offline-First Bug Tracker Embedded in Git, with Bridges | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=43971620\"},{\"title\":\"Git Internals: Objects, Refs, and the DAG - Library - Grizzly Peak Software\",\"url\":\"https://www.grizzlypeaksoftware.com/library/git-internals-objects-refs-and-the-dag-n5uojqz2\"},{\"title\":\"Git Internals: Objects, Refs & the DAG\",\"url\":\"https://cheatsheets.davidveksler.com/git-internals.html\"},{\"title\":\"Method and system for generating security findings acquisition records for systems and system components\",\"url\":\"https://image-ppubs.uspto.gov/dirsearch-public/print/downloadPdf/12001566\"},{\"title\":\"Part 10: Git Internals — The Object Model & DAG - Wasil Zafar\",\"url\":\"https://www.wasilzafar.com/pages/series/software-engineering/software-engineering-part10-git-internals.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about git-bug's entity operations DAG stored in git refs and its generic entity framework:\n\n## Generic Entity Framework\n\nThe entity framework makes it easy to extend git-bug, but also to use it as a library to create brand new applications using the same techniques as git-bug.\n\n## DAG for Operations\n\nOperations can now be represented in a DAG with concurrent editions across machines while still supporting proper merge conflict, instead of the enforced linear structure as before. This addresses limitations of the earlier approach, as things were working OK with a star topology of git remotes (that is, a central repository) but would break down with anything more complicated.\n\n## Data Model Improvements\n\nThe new data model also becomes fully immutable (aka append-only), which is much more conductive with cryptographic signatures and encryption.\n\n## Entity Package Architecture\n\nA reusable entity package is capable of handling all the complex operations of an Entity (bug, board, config ...): operations, DAG manipulation, conflict merge, signature, integrity ... to greatly simplify writing and maintaining an entity.\n\nThese enhancements enable git-bug to support distributed, offline-first operations with proper conflict resolution across multiple machines while maintaining data integrity through immutable operation logs.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MpYWMRXSs8zpd9122Wkct1","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"324e5de5bd856853a4c994915cf2b93c8a3d6e6b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-83f1da10d73d9620722a7e3e8ddd65a5b476dc78140b00a8dfde596c8d26a9c1","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.241"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-24T03:44:49.655Z","producer":{"tool":"cled