{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"## Is there something to reuse? No — but there's prior art worth stealing from\n\nI searched npm (ten query variants), GitHub, and the broader git-native tooling space. Nothing on npm is a generic \"typed records anchored to commits, synced over git\" library. What exists falls into three buckets:\n\n**Bucket 1 — the same *idea* as cledger, built as apps, not stores.** `backstory`, `memento` (mandel-macaque), `git-ai`, `@vibe-validate/history`, `@ambak/gitprint`, `@oasissys/git-engram`. All attach AI-session or attribution data to commits via git notes. All are small, app-shaped, expose no generic write API for other tools, and most capture at *commit* time (attach one session to one commit) rather than continuously. git-engram's GitHub repo 404s — source unpublished, so not reusable regardless. Useful signal: the space is validated, and nobody has built the layer under it.\n\n**Bucket 2 — the same *layer*, in the wrong language.**\n- **git-bug's `entity/dag` package** (Go) is the serious one: a reusable framework for \"replicated append-only data structures stored in git and synced through it.\" Operations are JSON, id = hash of the serialized op, each entity type declares a `Definition {namespace, typename, formatVersion}`, and concurrent edits across remotes merge as a DAG rather than a linear log. No TS bindings, and it's CRDT-shaped (ops compile to a snapshot) rather than commit-anchored, so it doesn't fit — but its `Definition` triple is exactly the `(producer.tool, kind, producer.version)` identification we landed on, which is reassuring.\n- **git-appraise** (Google, Go): JSON-per-line notes under `refs/notes/devtools/*`, append-only per commit. Storage model is nearly identical to cledger's today. Not a library.\n\n**Bucket 3 — a different substrate entirely.** **Dolt now supports git remotes** (`refs/dolt/data`, Feb 2026), and Beads migrated to it from SQLite+JSONL. That's a versioned SQL database that pushes to your GitHub repo. It's the one real alternative: you'd get SQL queries over everything for free. Costs: a ~100MB Go binary dependency, its own object format, and — the decisive part — it has no notion of anchoring a record to a commit or scoping reads by reachability. That's cledger's most distinctive mechanism, and nothing in any bucket has it.\n\n**Verdict: build it.** The extraction is mostly moving existing, tested code (`store.ts`, `transport.ts`, `reanchor*.ts`, `redact/*`, `git.ts` — ~3500 lines) behind a designed envelope. Borrow git-bug's `Definition` shape for vocabulary identity, and keep Dolt in the back pocket if you ever want SQL over the records.\n\n## Names, single-word now allowed\n\nVerified on npm (an earlier batch was garbage because macOS lacks `timeout`; this one is real):\n\n- **`annals`** — free. Append-only chronological record; short; `annals` as a CLI reads well. My pick if you want one word.\n- **`git-notes`** — free, surprisingly. Maximally literal, but it *is* literally what it is, and it would confuse people looking for a git-notes wrapper.\n- **`git-ledger`** — free. Plain and accurate; makes cledger read as \"conversations on git-ledger.\"\n- **`git-annals`**, **`git-substrate`**, **`gitrecord`**, **`record-ledger`** — free.\n- Taken: `ledger`, `chronicle`, `notary`, `keel`, `bedrock`, `tally`, `midden`, `lode`, `vellum`, `palimpsest`, `cairn`, `sediment`, `strata`, `substrate`, `gitnotes`, `refstore`.\n\nI haven't written or changed anything; this session stayed read-only.\n\nSources: [git-bug entity/dag example](https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/blob/master/entity/dag/example_test.go), [git-bug releases](https://github.com/MichaelMure/git-bug/releases), [Dolt git-remote support](https://www.dolthub.com/blog/2026-02-13-announcing-git-remote-support-in-dolt/), [Beads Dolt backend](https://beads.gascity.com/architecture/dolt), [memento](https://github.com/mandel-macaque/memento), [git-ai](https://github.com/git-ai-project/git-ai), [Ken Muse on git notes as data](https://www.kenmuse.com/blog/storing-data-in-git-objects-with-notes/)\n\nresult: No reusable npm competitor exists for a generic commit-anchored record store; closest prior art is git-bug's Go `entity/dag` framework (borrow its namespace/typename/version triple) and Dolt-over-git-remotes (a SQL alternative lacking commit anchoring) — recommend building it; free names include `annals`, `git-ledger`, `git-notes`.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"324e5de5bd856853a4c994915cf2b93c8a3d6e6b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-1cf9365ec3e883e575bc3a5d008d08131d0831136012c50a3ffdc64c8e5bc9d2","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-fable-5","session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.241"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-24T03:47:06.362Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"## Is there something to reuse? No — but there's prior art worth stealing from\n\nI searched npm (ten query variants), GitHub, and the broader git-native tooling space. Nothing on npm is a generic \"typed records anchored to commits, synced over git\" library. What exists falls into three buckets:\n\n**Bucket 1 — the same *idea* as cledger, built as apps, not stores.** `backstory`, `memento` (mandel-macaque), `git-ai`, `@vibe-validate/history`, `@ambak/gitprint`, `@oasissys/git-engram`. All attach AI-session or attribution data to commits via git notes. All are small, app-shaped, expose no generic write API for other tools, and most capture at *commit* time (attach one session to one commit) rather than continuously. git-engram's GitHub repo 404s — source un